	// No CLI equivalent — the CLI has direct database access and can just run `wpcalc token create` again instead. Public: a refresh token is presented in the request body, not as a bearer credential, precisely so this is reachable once an access token has already expired. Single-use — the refresh token given here stops working the instant this succeeds, whether or not the caller keeps the newly rotated one; reusing an already-exchanged refresh token is treated the same as an unknown one (401), not specially flagged, so a client cannot use the response to probe whether a given secret was ever valid.
